From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: reset after an MCU timeout only once the
 device is registered

A message timeout queues a full chip reset. During probe, a timeout of a
firmware download or init command queues it for a device that mac80211
has not registered and that the probe error path is tearing down, and
the reset work then runs on freed or half-initialized state.

mt7996_reset() already ignores requests until hw_init_done is set; do
the same for the reset on a message timeout.

Fixes: d2b860454ea2 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: reset device after MCU message timeout")
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/1147
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/1148
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -231,7 +231,9 @@ mt7996_mcu_parse_response(struct mt76_de
 		dev_err(mdev->dev, "Message %08x (seq %d) timeout\n",
 			cmd, seq);
 
-		if (!test_and_set_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state)) {
+		/* a full reset needs a registered device */
+		if (dev->recovery.hw_init_done &&
+		    !test_and_set_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state)) {
 			dev->recovery.restart = true;
 			wake_up(&dev->mt76.mcu.wait);
 			queue_work(dev->mt76.wq, &dev->reset_work);
